-- | Lowers a `.psx` module to ordinary PureScript.
-- |
-- | The lowering splices: plain PureScript and the expressions in holes are
-- | copied verbatim, and each markup literal is replaced by calls to the
-- | backend module the file imports, under the alias `B`:
-- |
-- | - an element is `B.<name> [ attrs ] (children)`, or `B.element "<name>"`
-- |   for a name the HTML table does not have, and `B.none` stands for no
-- |   children;
-- | - a child hole is `B.children (e)`. Whether the children are keyed is
-- |   their type's business: the backend's `Children` instances say what a
-- |   hole's value makes, keyed or not, and its element functions take either
-- |   (decision 3 on #23);
-- | - an attribute is the table's function for it (`B.class_`, `B.onClick`),
-- |   or `B.attribute "<name>"` for one the table does not have;
-- | - a trait hole `{e}` among the attributes is `(e)`, one element of the
-- |   attribute array. Attributes are always one array literal, never a
-- |   concatenation, so purs holds a trait hole to exactly one `Attr`. An
-- |   `Attr` can't change its element's type, so a key can't go in a trait
-- |   hole unless the framework keys by an attribute of the element itself
-- |   (Portico's `P.key`), and the lowering doesn't track one that does;
-- | - text is `B.text "..."` after the whitespace policy
-- |   (`Psx.Lower.Whitespace`) and character references;
-- | - a literal denotes `Markup a`, an array of nodes, and a literal whose
-- |   root carries `key` denotes an array of `B.keyed k node`. A key
-- |   belongs to the parent's child list, not to the element: keyed
-- |   children are what make the parent a keyed element.
-- |
-- | Lowering preserves lines: each piece of markup's code starts on the line
-- | the markup is on, and each hole's expression on its own line, at its own
-- | column when the generated code before it is short enough. The header
-- | line and the `B` import take the place of blank lines in the import
-- | section when there are any. `Psx.Lower.PositionMap` records the rest.
module Psx.Lower
  ( Lowered
  , Style
  , lower
  , lowerPsxt
  , backendModules
  , header
  , isGenerated
  ) where

